From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover the vendored GraphBLAS licence

`license-files = ["LICENSE"]` is an explicit PEP 639 list, so it does not
fall back to a `LICENSE*` auto-discovery glob: a `LICENSE.graphblas`
dropped at the project root to cover the SuiteSparse:GraphBLAS C library
that `auditwheel repair` vendors into the wheel (built from source, see
`suitesparse.sh`) is silently ignored. Widening the list to also match
`LICENSE.*` picks it up with no other packaging change.

Upstream's own wheels (manylinux_2_28/macOS/Windows) carry the same gap:
only LICENSE ships in dist-info/licenses, with no notice for GraphBLAS
itself or the lz4/zstd/xxHash sources it bundles.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against GraphBLAS/python-suitesparse-graphblas]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 15dee86..8237536 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ description = "SuiteSparse:GraphBLAS Python bindings."
 readme = "README.md"
 requires-python = ">=3.11"
 license = "Apache-2.0"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE", "LICENSE.*"]
 authors = [
     {name = "Erik Welch", email = "erik.n.welch@gmail.com"},
     {name = "Jim Kitchen"},
--
2.43.0
